                    briefing_title_r1:      `Round 1 — Diagnose the reputation gap`,
                    briefing_text_r1:       `A consumer influencer alleges the flagship seasoning hides an undeclared additive. In 18 hours the video has <strong>2.4M views</strong>, two chains holding <strong>31% of modern trade</strong> have delisted, week-one sales are down <strong>22%</strong>, <strong>89%</strong> of mentions are negative, and the reputation tracker has fallen from <strong>72 to 51</strong> in 72 hours. This is not just a PR fire — it is a <em>coherence failure</em>. Three things no longer align: the stated identity (“all-natural, family-trusted”), the actual substance (a permitted-but-undisclosed additive), and the construed image (what people now believe). Name the true threat, locate the gap that matters, and separate the genuine substance problem from the perception problem.`,
                    briefing_title_r2:      `Round 2 — Align the identity before you communicate`,
                    briefing_text_r2:       `You cannot message your way out of an identity that no longer holds. The label says “all-natural”; the product carries a permitted additive that was never clearly disclosed. Decide what Zuriel <em>actually</em> stands for now — reframe to “safe, transparent, trusted,” defend the natural claim by reformulating, hold and contest, or reposition entirely — and decide whether substance must change (reformulate or relabel) to make the new identity true. Test it against 35 years of “Nourishing Nigerian families since 1991”: a coherent evolution preserves equity; <strong>a panic rebrand erases it</strong>.`,
                    briefing_title_r3:      `Round 3 — Choose communication actions within ₦600M`,
                    briefing_text_r3:       `Deploy the <strong>₦600M</strong> across the action menu and sequence it against the 5-day window. In a trust crisis, <em>who vouches for you matters more than how loud you are</em> — independent certification and a traceability microsite buy proof; paid advertising only buys reach. Choose a spokesperson tone, and keep one consistent message across consumers, retailers, NAFDAC, employees and investors. Three different statements side by side on social media is itself a signal of evasion — and if the say–do gap is still open, every Naira of “trust us” advertising broadcasts the exact gap that caused this.`,
